  "body": {
    "id": "thm:path-bands",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "For every admissible compact family \\(\\mathcal K\\) and every \\(\\varepsilon>0\\),\n\\[\n \\sup_{Q\\in\\mathcal K}P_{N,Q}\\!\\left(\\left\\|\\sqrt N[\\widehat\\theta_T-\\theta_T]_Q-N^{-1/2}\\sum_{i=1}^N[\\psi_{\\theta,T}(\\xi_i)]_Q\\right\\|>\\varepsilon\\right)\\to0.\n\\]\nThe limiting vector is \\([D\\Psi_T(\\beta_0,\\sigma^2,\\tau^2,P_{0X})[\\mathcal A_T\\mathbb Z_T^{\\mathrm{full}}]]_Q\\sim\\mathcal N(0,[\\Omega_\\theta]_Q)\\).  The observable covariance estimator is uniformly consistent for exactly this influence covariance: for every \\(\\varepsilon>0\\), \\(\\sup_{Q\\in\\mathcal K}P_{N,Q}(\\|[\\widehat\\Omega_\\theta-\\Omega_\\theta]_Q\\|>\\varepsilon)\\to0\\).  If, in addition, \\(\\inf_{Q\\in\\mathcal K}\\max_{1\\le t\\le T}[\\Omega_{\\theta,tt}]_Q>0\\), then\n\\[\n \\liminf_{N\\to\\infty}\\inf_{Q\\in\\mathcal K}P_{N,Q}\\{[\\theta_{T,t}]_Q\\in[\\mathcal C_{N,t}]_Q\\text{ for every }1\\le t\\le T\\}\\ge1-\\alpha.\n\\]\nEquality holds pointwise at any \\(Q\\) for which the maximum absolute coordinate of \\(\\mathcal N(0,[\\Omega_\\theta]_Q)\\) has a continuous nondegenerate distribution.",
